WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Welcome to Share Your Bitcoin Journey,
presented by Bitcoin for the Arts.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
I'm Dion Wilson, the founder and executive
director of Bitcoin for the Arts, the first 501[c][3] nonprofit funding artists with Bitcoin grants, education, and sovereign funding tools.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Today, we have the pleasure of speaking
with a conceptual multimedia artist, classically trained in London, who walked away from the arts establishment in both London and Reykjavik out of frustration with the status quo, and who now lives with his wife and children in the mountains of central Italy, quietly producing some of the most rigorous fine art anywhere in the Bitcoin space today.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
His practice carries a two-word tagline:
Depicting Bitcoin. He has folded his entire artistic identity into that single subject, and it has, in his own words,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:12.000
given purpose to both his art and his life
in general.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:24.000
His most consequential work to date is a
monumental oil painting titled The Whole Entire Universe, which debuted at the Bitcoin 2026 conference in Las Vegas.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:36.000
His work is being collected and exhibited
in what feels like the emerging citadels of Bitcoin: Lugano Plan B in Switzerland, The Venetian in Las Vegas, a planned monumental public sculpture in Roatán in the offshore Bitcoin community there.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:48.000
This is not the museum circuit.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:00.000
This is a new patronage geography built by
Bitcoiners for Bitcoiners, and Anik is already one of its most serious inhabitants In this conversation, we go back to the beginning, classical training in London,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:12.000
and what that forge gave him that he still
uses every day. The disillusionment that pulled him first to Reykjavik, and then to the mountains of Italy.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:24.000
How Bitcoin first clicked, and why it
became not just a subject, but the subject of his entire practice.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:36.000
The math and the meaning behind the whole
entire universe, building an artistic household with his wife and children.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:48.000
The question of what a renaissance in
serious craft looks like when it happens outside of MoMA and inside of Lugano, Roatán, and a studio in a mountain village.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:03:00.000
And what it means to be a father making
work today in a sound monetary system designed with the next generation in mind. Without further ado, welcome to the show

